# SAMPO2 Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the architecture for "SAMPO2", a modular algorithmic trading research pipeline.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Action Space Config**: The action space is hardcoded as discrete: `HOLD_OUT`, `BUY`, `SELL`, `CLOSE`, `HOLD_IN`. Ensure this maps logic correctly to your broker execution later.
> **Dependency Handling**: We assume a Python environment with `gymnasium`, `stable-baselines3`, `tensorflow`, [arch](file:///c:/Users/Jeff/Desktop/SAMPO%20project%20folder/sampo2/pipeline/system_architecture_pipeline.py#79-86) (for GARCH), and `pandas`.
> **Data Source**: We will use [combined_data.csv](file:///c:/Users/Jeff/Desktop/sample_DS/SAMPO/combined_data.csv) from the `SAMPO` directory as the primary input for now. Future live data will be sourced from **Interactive Brokers** (replacing OANDA).

## Proposed Architecture

We will create a python package `sampo2` with the following structure:

```
sampo2/
├── __init__.py
├── config.py               # Global configuration (paths, params)
├── data/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── loader.py           # Data loading & validation
│   ├── garch.py            # GARCH volatility modeling
│   └── processor.py        # Dataset merging & preprocessing
├── models/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── pnn.py              # Parallel Neural Network (TensorFlow)
├── env/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── trading_env.py      # Gymnasium Trading Environment
│   └── actions.py          # Action constants used globally
├── agents/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   └── trainer.py          # PPO Training & Evaluation (SB3)
└── utils/
    ├── __init__.py
    └── logger.py           # Logging utilities
```

Root scripts:
- [run_pipeline.py](file:///c:/Users/Jeff/Desktop/sample_DS/run_pipeline.py): Main CLI entry point.

